{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785868193,"nonce":"ia2TtM8gD6kOOkvIJwCc8a10C50=","title":"b4 send: multi-line [bracket] annotation between trailers gets moved into commit prose","message":"Reported-by: Luigi Leonardi \u003cleonardi@redhat.com\u003e\nLink: https://lore.kernel.org/CANo9s6mjy57bsiib_+BhpftUZ73=Nwg35VK_v+ebt_KK-yf9Bg@mail.gmail.com\n\n\nWhile backporting a patch to stable, Luigi added a backporter annotation\nbetween the two Signed-off-bys:\n\n    Signed-off-by: Paolo Abeni \u003cpabeni@redhat.com\u003e\n    [LL: something something\n    that wraps to a second line]\n    Signed-off-by: Luigi Leonardi \u003cleonardi@redhat.com\u003e\n\n`b4 send` silently relocated the [LL: ...] block up into the commit\nprose, leaving the two SoBs together at the bottom:\n\n- intended: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260515-linux-6-6-y-v1-1-b47eaf4cc6e6@redhat.com/\n- mangled:  https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260515-linux-5-15-y-v1-1-033f2ea86d6c@redhat.com/\n\nHe asked for an option to disable the reordering.\n\n\n`LoreMessage.find_trailers()` (src/b4/__init__.py:2818), which every\nbody rebuild goes through:\n\n- A bracketed comment following a trailer IS supported -- but only when\n  it fits on ONE line. The check at src/b4/__init__.py:2915 is\n  `re.search(r'^\\s*\\[[^]]+]\\s*$', line)`: opening `[` and closing `]`\n  must be on the same line, in which case the comment is attached to\n  the preceding trailer as extinfo and survives in place (verified).\n\n- A WRAPPED bracket comment matches nothing: line one has no closing\n  `]`, line two has no opening `[`, so both lines fall into `others`\n  (body prose) and `was_trailer` resets. When `rebuild_message()`\n  reassembles the body as message + trailers, the comment ends up above\n  both SoBs -- exactly what Luigi saw.\n\n- src/b4/__init__.py:2843-2847 contains a commented-out regex that\n  unwrapped exactly this multi-line-bracket case; it was disabled as\n  \"too false-positivey\".\n\n\nFor a multi-patch series, patch bodies from `git show --format=email`\ngo out untouched. Both of Luigi's backports are single-patch,\ncoverless series, so `mixin_cover()` (src/b4/ez.py:2235) folds the\ncover into the patch -- and that path does get_body_parts() -\u003e\nrebuild_message() on the patch body, triggering the relocation. The\nsame hazard exists in every other body-rebuild path (fix_trailers()\nfor `b4 trailers -u`, `b4 am` with follow-up trailers, etc).\n\n\nFix the parser rather than add a \"don't reorder\" knob (the rebuild is\ninherent to mixin_cover/fix_trailers, there is no single reordering\nstep to disable, and trailer-order support was already removed once in\n87ef713). In the find_trailers line loop: when `was_trailer` is set\nand a line starts with `[` but has no closing `]`, accumulate\ncontinuation lines until the one ending in `]`, and attach the joined\ntext as extinfo to the preceding trailer. Gating on \"immediately\nfollows a trailer\" plus \"must terminate with `]`\" avoids the\nfalse-positive swamp that killed the old blanket regex, since any\nblank line resets was_trailer. Needs a check that multi-line extinfo\nround-trips sanely through LoreTrailer.as_string().","files":null}]}